<title>UK: SOCCER-NORWAY'S FJORTOFT LEAVES MIDDLESBROUGH.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-NORWAY'S FJORTOFT LEAVES MIDDLESBROUGH.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian striker Jan-Aage Fjortoft left premier league Middlesbrough to join English first division Sheffield United for 700,000 pounds ($1.1 million) on Friday.</p>
<p>Fjortoft, who lost his place at Middlesbrough with the arrival of Italian Fabrizio Ravanelli and Dane Mikkel Beck, leaves a side propping up the top flight to join a United team second in the first division and pushing hard for promotion.</p>
<p>He is expected to make his United debut against Swindon, his first club in England, on Saturday.</p>
</text>
